common: skip variable tracking for the about banner

buildKicadAboutBanner() is one enormous run of generated string appends;
compiled with optimization and debug info its SSA graph exceeds GCC's
max-vartrack-size limit, so GCC abandons -fvar-tracking-assignments for
it anyway -- after a wasted first compile attempt and a diagnostic:

  AboutDialog_main.cpp:58:13: note: variable tracking size limit
  exceeded with '-fvar-tracking-assignments', retrying without

Starting the file without VTA produces identical debug info while
skipping the doomed attempt and its note. Guarded to GCC: clang has no
such option.

diff --git a/common/CMakeLists.txt b/common/CMakeLists.txt
index c362888c0c..16f7f905d0 100644
--- a/common/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/common/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -491,6 +491,17 @@ set( COMMON_ABOUT_DLG_SRCS
     dialog_about/dialog_about_base.cpp
     )
 
+if( CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID STREQUAL "GNU" )
+    # buildKicadAboutBanner() is one enormous run of generated string appends;
+    # with optimization and debug info its SSA graph exceeds GCC's
+    # max-vartrack-size, so GCC abandons -fvar-tracking-assignments for it
+    # anyway -- after a wasted first attempt and a "variable tracking size
+    # limit exceeded" note. Starting without VTA produces the same debug info
+    # minus the retry and the note.
+    set_source_files_properties( dialog_about/AboutDialog_main.cpp PROPERTIES
+        COMPILE_OPTIONS "-fno-var-tracking-assignments" )
+endif()
+
 set( COMMON_GIT_DLG_SRCS
     dialogs/git/dialog_git_commit.cpp
     dialogs/git/dialog_git_switch.cpp
